WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:02.720
INTRO:
Eversince Russia invaded Ukraine, much of

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:07.559
the western world has bombarded them with
restrictions, boycotts, and sanctions.

00:00:07.559 --> 00:00:13.080
For example, the biggest companies in the
world including Apple, Amazon, Adobe, Netflix,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.910
and Disney have all stopped operations in
Russia.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.140
Similarly, many countries have stopped importing
Russian oil, and some countries wont even

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.490
let Russian aircraft fly over them.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.200
Not to mention, most Russian banks and accounts
have been completely frozen.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.290
The idea was that we could help Ukraine by
hurting Russia economically and that an economic

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.720
crash would cause Russia to back out faster.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.430
But, so far this doesn’t seem to be the
case.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.940
The Russian economy is indeed hurting, but
the Russian Ruble is actually stronger than

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.940
ever.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.840
And if you don’t believe me, just take a
look at the charts.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.100
Initially, the Ruble did crash 50% as soon
as the sanctions were implemented, but since

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.540
then, Ruble has skyrocketed 150%.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.040
This means that the Ruble is currently the
strongest its been in 7 years.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.329
Now, you might be thinking that this must
be because the dollar is performing even worse

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:06.759
or something like that.

00:01:06.759 --> 00:01:08.850
But, this isn’t the case either.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:13.689
In fact, the dollar is the strongest its been
in 20 years on a relative basis.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:17.969
And this just makes it even more significant
that the Russian Ruble is skyrocketing against

00:01:17.969 --> 00:01:19.139
the dollar.

00:01:19.139 --> 00:01:23.579
So, what in the world is happening with the
Russian Ruble and why is it mooning despite

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:24.719
all the sanctions.

00:01:24.719 --> 00:01:30.570
INEFFECTIVE SANCTIONS:
One of the top reasons that the Ruble is doing

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.950
so well is because many of the sanctions imposed
on Russia aren’t even that effective, especially

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.700
the energy sanctions.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.369
You see, the European Union is way more dependent
on Russian energy than they would like to

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:43.369
admit.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.700
And though I’m sure many of them would like
to ban Russian imports completely, this is

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.999
simply not realistic.

00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:52.889
Here’s the thing, Russia is the world’s
largest gas exporter and the second largest

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:53.899
oil exporter.

00:01:53.899 --> 00:01:58.659
So, it’s not really possible to completely
cut off Russian exports overnight.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:02.770
If they did do this, it would be the countries
that are importing oil that would collapse

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:03.770
first.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.520
But, wait a minute, didn’t the EU implement
a Russian oil embargo?

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.420
Well, the answer is yes, but there’s a lot
of fine print and exceptions.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.769
First of all, the goal is to ban most imports
by the end of the year, not by tomorrow.

00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:22.540
Also, certain countries like Slovenia and
Hungary are partially or even completely exempt

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.760
from the embargo.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.280
Such countries are not only extremely dependent
on Russian exports, but more importantly,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.120
they’re landlocked meaning that they can’t
receive oil through the sea.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.480
These countries primarily get their oil through
pipelines directly from Russia, and as you

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.569
would guess, rebuilding such infrastructure
would take several years if not well over

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:41.650
a decade.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.829
And given that most western countries are
already headed towards a recession, completely

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:49.830
uprooting their crude oil source is the last
thing these countries want to do.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:54.320
And given that oil prices are skyrocketing
as well, energy exports have just become even

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.920
more profitable for Russia.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.069
In fact, during the first 100 days of the
war, it’s estimated that Russia pulled in

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:03.870
$60 billion worth of revenue from fossil fuel
exports to the EU alone.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.340
Also, let’s not forget that not every country
is against Russia.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:13.629
Most of us are constantly exposed to western
media, so it seems like the entire world is

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:17.709
against Russia, but this isn’t true by any
means.

00:03:17.709 --> 00:03:23.930
Many countries actually support the war including
Belarus, Cuba, Nicaragua, Venezuela, and Kyrgystan.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.959
But, you don’t even have to support Russia
to help them.

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:31.549
If you simply stay neutral and continue importing
Russian oil, that itself is a massive benefit

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:32.849
for Russia.

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:37.209
And this is exactly what many countries have
been doing, particularly China and India.

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:40.959
This countries have no financial reason to
stop importing Russian energy.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:43.769
In fact, their incentivized to import more.

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:47.969
You see, as western countries slowly step
away from Russian energy, the price of Russian

00:03:47.969 --> 00:03:52.469
energy decreases, and this gives countries
like China and India the perfect oppurtunity

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:56.340
to buy for a discount and that’s exactly
what they’ve been doing.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.749
China has risen to be Russia’s top oil importer
having bought $12.6 billion worth of oil since

00:04:00.749 --> 00:04:02.109
the war started.

00:04:02.109 --> 00:04:06.030
Meanwhile, India has transitioned from being
an occasional buyer to being a consistent

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.030
buyer.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.209
Before the war started, India imported well
below 5 million barrels of oil from Russia

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:14.099
on a monthly basis, and many months were even
0.

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:18.080
But now, India is importing tens of millions
of barrels worth of oil every month.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.910
And as more time passes, I think its just
even more likely that more countries adopt

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.910
such a policy.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.410
It’s not that they support the war.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.670
Rather, they’re simply gonna do what’s
in their best interest.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.610
And if Russia has the cheapest oil, then so
be it.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:37.420
SUPPLY &amp; DEMAND:
Aside from western sanctions being negated

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:42.350
by exemptions and neutral countries, the Ruble
is also substantially benefitting from supply

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.350
and demand.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.040
While we like to throw around a bunch of fancy
terms like quantitive easing when describing

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.140
a country’s currency or economy, in the
end, the currency’s strength just comes

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.900
down to supply and demand.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.430
If demand outpaces supply, then the currency
will gain dominance.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:01.160
Conversely, if supply outpaces demand, then
the currency will lose dominance.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.510
Western countries were obviously trying to
accomplish the latter by eliminating demand,

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.970
but this has sort of backfired.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.630
As we just discussed, Russia is still able
to find significant amounts of demand for

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:15.060
their oil which in turn means the Ruble is
in high demand.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:19.380
However, the supply of Rubles has gone down
substantially because almost every western

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.770
company you can think of has left Russia.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.030
So, Russians are no longer giving Rubles to
foreign companies.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:30.520
If you haven’t noticed yet, this means that
Rubles are entering Russia but not leaving

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:31.520
Russia.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.890
Russia has actually leaned into this by implementing
a slew of different rules.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:39.320
For example, Putin has declared that importing
countries must pay for Russian oil and natural

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.010
gas using Rubles.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:45.160
Similarly, Russian exporters are required
to convert atleast half of their excess revenues

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.470
into Rubles.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.890
These rules stretch further than just exports
and imports as well.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.680
For instance, Russia has banned foreign stock
and bond holders from taking their dividend

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.350
payments out of Russia.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:59.540
All of these policies have just further inflated
the demand for the Ruble while also deflating

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.240
the supply of the Ruble.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.490
And simple economics would tell you that this
is extremely beneficial for the Ruble.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:09.870
Not to mention, Russians themselves are extremely
reluctant to let go of their Rubles because

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.590
they can earn extraordinary interest rates
by just leaving it in the bank.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.330
When the war started, Russia hiked interest
rates all the way to 20%.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.660
They have since decreased them to 10%, but
as long as the currency itself is holding

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:25.010
strong, there’s very little reason to seek
out investments or spend your money when you

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.380
can just earn 10% doing nothing.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:31.120
Russia has actually started to lighten such
monetary policies because they also don’t

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.900
want the Ruble to get too strong.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:37.280
You see, if the Ruble continues to get stronger,
exports from the country will become less

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:41.340
and less appealing, and that’s the last
thing Russia wants right now.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:46.160
So, ironically, the Ruble is starting to get
so strong that even Russia is ok with a slight

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.640
cool down.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:53.280
A GOLDEN CAGE:
Listening to all of this, it might seem like

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.590
westerns sanctions were a massive fail, and
from one perspective, they were.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:01.860
After all, Russia is still making loads of
money and their currency is stronger than

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:02.860
ever.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.830
But, it’s not all sunshines and rainbows.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:09.360
While Russia has plenty of money to spend,
they can’t actually spend it.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:13.430
Here’s the thing, while sanctions may not
have been that efffective at stopping countries

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:17.530
from buying Russian products, they have been
quite successful at preventing Russia from

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:18.770
buyign foreign products.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.470
A great example of this is car sales.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:24.500
Russia expects car sales to half by the end
of the year.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.140
Another example is semiconductors.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:30.890
In fact, the supply of semiconductors has
gotten so bad in Russia that they have started

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:34.300
to use dishwasher and refrigerator chips inside
military equipment.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.960
This isn’t that surprising when you consider
that US technology exports to Russia have

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.900
decreased by 70% since the start of the war.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.400
This is the same case telecommunications,
lasers, avionics, and maritime technology

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.520
as well.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:50.580
And while Russia may be able to put up a strong
facade in the short term, it’s only a matter

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.770
of time until these internal shortages start
destroying not just their economy but their

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.140
entire society.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:59.180
But wait a minute, doesn’t everything get
produced in China?

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:03.320
Why don’t Chinese companies just supply
Russians with semiconductors and phones and

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.320
cars?

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.670
Not to mention, they could probably charge
the Russians a premium for this right?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:12.720
Well, they definitely could, but none of the
big Chinese companies really want to do this.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.250
This isn’t that say that these companies
support Ukraine, but at the same time, helping

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.070
Russia isn’t in their best interest either.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:23.330
Here’s the thing, these manufacturing companies
have insanely large contracts with American

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.880
juggernauts like Apple and Nvidia.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:29.950
And the last thing they want to do is jeopardize
their contracts with these companies by selling

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.380
equipment to Russia.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.650
It’s simply not worth the risk.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.270
This isn’t to say that no one is helping
Russia though.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.180
Many smaller companies that don’t have relationships
with western countries and companies are willing

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.180
to help Russia.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:45.350
But, as you would guess, these are almost
always second grade products.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:49.360
So, the longer these sanctions go on, the
more likely it is that Russia’s technology

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.580
will degrade.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.900
Aside from facing an internal supply crisis,
Russia is also facing a debt crisis.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:59.360
Recently, Russia missed a bond interest payment,
not because they couldn’t afford it but

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.980
because they couldn’t pay.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:05.630
You see, the interest payments were supposed
to be in Euros and Dollars, but Russia doesn’t

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.490
really have access to these currencies.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:12.420
So, they tried paying with Rubles but this
payment was blocked by international sanctions.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:16.490
Considering this, missing the payment isn’t
exactly Russia’s fault, but this will no

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:20.130
doubt discourage investors from buying Russian
bonds which will just make it even harder

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.020
for Russia to get through this war.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:26.570
So, while the Ruble is stronger than ever,
the same cannot be said about the Russian

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:27.570
economy.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:33.190
THE STATE OF RUSSIA:
At the end of the day, Russia has played the

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.350
sanctions game as well as they can.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:40.030
They’ve found new buyers for their oil,
they’ve limited the outflow of Rubles, and

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:42.440
they’ve successfully stabilized the currency.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.560
All of these efforts have kept Russian income
rather consistent, but this isn’t to say

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.820
that Russia is winning the economic war.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:53.500
While Russia has plenty of money to spend,
they literally can’t spend it.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.810
They can’t buy cars or phones or computers
or really anything.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:10:00.740
They’re forced to rely Chinese knockoffs
that don’t have anything to lose by working

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:01.760
with them.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.190
This hans’t become that big of a problem
yet given that the sanctions have only been

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.040
in place for a few months.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.900
But imagine what happens 5 years down the
line.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.680
What will everyday Russians do when they need
a new car or a new computer.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.862
Russia’s tech industry has already realized
this, and that why tens of thousands of tech

00:10:17.862 --> 00:10:20.010
workers have been fleeing the country.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:24.140
And as these tech workers flee the country,
it just becomes even less likely that Russia

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.150
is able to reproduce western technology by
themselves.

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:31.390
And in today’s world where technology is
basically an essential, Russia will only be

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:34.800
able to keep up this charade for so long until
something gives.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:40.440
So yes, the Russian Ruble is indeed the best
performing currency of 2022, but in the end,

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.770
the entire point of currency is to act as
a medium of exchange.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:48.710
And given that the Ruble is failing at doing
just that, it’s relative strength is all

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.710
but meaningful.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.400
But that’s just what I think.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:54.220
How much longer do you think Russia can keep
up this charade?

